# Patterns here match TARGET paths under $HOME that chezmoi should NOT manage.
# (The repo README, docs/, packages/, etc. live above the source root — set by
# .chezmoiroot -> "home" — so they never reach $HOME and need no entry here.)

# fish's universal-variable store is runtime state, not config: fish rewrites it
# on upgrade, fisher on plugin changes, the theme sync on every mode flip. A
# tracked snapshot goes stale and regresses other machines on apply (it carried
# the jethrokuan/z plugin record long after .chezmoiremove dropped z). Anything
# that must hold everywhere belongs in config.fish instead.
.config/fish/fish_variables

# Noctalia regenerates this on every theme change (see zathurarc). zathura treats
# the missing include as a non-fatal warning, so a fresh machine needs no seed —
# unlike niri's noctalia.kdl, which is a `create_` file for exactly that reason.
.config/zathura/noctaliarc

# Noctalia v5 config is tracked on every profile: 00-base.toml (machine-agnostic)
# + palettes/ ship everywhere, and 10-machine.toml.tmpl branches per `.machine`
# (monitors, wallpaper, DPI). The per-output wallpaper darkman hook is likewise a
# `.tmpl` that branches per machine. Nothing here is home-only any more.
# See docs/adr/0020 (supersedes 0012).
